module gunbc.roadmap.belt_concurrency

import std.nat { Nat, Succ, Zero }

// THE SRV1 LAB'S BELT WIDTH, AS A LEAF, SO BOTH SIDES READ ONE COPY (§3). The per-instance belt concurrency
// is carried on HostDashboardInstance.belt_max_concurrent (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dashboard_instance); the
// srv1 lab widens it to the figure defined here. It lives in THIS leaf -- importing std only -- because two
// sides need the same number and only one of them can reach the instance module: the instance rows read the
// Int form, and the live-deploy attempt-worker slice (gunbc.live_deploy.slice_bounds) charges a Nat slot
// count sized to srv1's widest belt so its workers actually fit. slice_bounds cannot import
// roadmap_dashboard_instance (the instance module reaches slice_bounds through host layout), so the number
// cannot live only there without closing an import cycle. The canonical value is the Nat below; the Int the
// instance and belt read is DERIVED from it by nat_to_int, so the figure has exactly one source.
//
// WHY srv1 HOLDS SIX. srv1 is a 512 GiB machine with about 245 GiB MemAvailable observed 2026-11-04 08:10Z.
// The worker ceiling is dispatch_worker_memory_ceiling = 22 GiB (gunbc_runner_slot_desired().memory_max).
// Six workers hold 6 x 22 = 132 GiB, which fits beside srv1-live's own belt (3 x 22 = 66 GiB) and srv1's
// compute build pool (compute_pool_slots x 22 = 2 x 22 = 44 GiB): 132 + 66 + 44 = 242 GiB <= 245 GiB, a
// 3 GiB margin. Seven would need 7 x 22 + 66 + 44 = 264 GiB > 245 and does NOT fit, so 6 is the largest belt
// the arithmetic allows; the srv1 fabric router's route ceiling is 8 (gunb-ai/gunbc#15789), so 6 is within it.
data srv1_lab_belt_max_concurrent_nat: Nat =
  Succ { prev: Succ { prev: Succ { prev: Succ { prev: Succ { prev: Succ { prev: Zero } } } } } }
